id=a52sxq_tethering_trains
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Tethering train BPF coverage guard
author=kusti420
description=Our BPF loader never loads the APEX's netd.o but /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.<active Tethering versionCode>.o, or a52_netd.o when the ROM ships no such object, whatever Tethering APEX Google Play has activated, and that APEX's system_server/netd code aborts if a map or program pin its own netd.o defines is missing or sized differently (crash loop; apexd reverts a fresh update, but a ROM flashed under an already active train has no such safety net). known/ holds the netd.o of the factory Tethering and of every Play train seen in the field (<versionCode>_<label>_netd.o; struct bpf_map_def is 192 bytes up to 26Q3 and 180 since the 26Q4 train 373041100, both understood). The build aborts unless the object the loader picks for each of them defines every map with the same definition (key/value size and max_entries included; ringbuf min_kver lowered to 5.4 by regen.py and 5.10+-only maps excepted) and pins every program they would pin on 5.4.302 at API 37, so a regenerated object can never silently drop a train that phones already run. The other objects the frozen loader takes from the active APEX (offload.o, test.o, clatd.o, dscpPolicy.o; critical, a failed load = reboot,bpfloader-failed loop) are checked too: each known entry needs its <versionCode>_<label>_<obj>.o, and on 5.4.302 at API 37 every map they would create must have a 5.4 map type, every program they would load a 5.4 program type and only 5.4 helpers/instructions, and every pin they define for API 37 must get created unless the factory object does not create it either or known/tolerated.txt lists it. Ships the list as /system/etc/bpf/a52_netd.known for k4-mainline-diag. Runtime half for a train nobody has seen yet: /system/bin/k4-tethering-gate (k4_tethering_gate.rc, domain k4apexdm) runs at load-bpf-programs on an update boot, after the evidence capture and before the loader: an activated Tethering whose versionCode is not in a52_netd.known is unsupported (its objects may need loader or kernel features 5.4 lacks: the 26Q4 train's layout change SIGABRTed the old loader -> reboot,bpfloader-failed loop on 2026-11-02), and so is a known one whose netd.o map pins the object picked for it lacks; either sets sys.k4.tethering_gap and the rc sets sys.init.updatable_crashing(_process_name=netd), the property apexd polls while a staged session is active, so apexd reverts the update and reboots once - instead of the bpfloader reboot loop or the netd/system_server crash loop, RescueParty / bootchecker escalation and the revert after several reboots of 2026-10-10. k4-mainline-diag names the gate as the reason (su -v) from the kmsg kept in /cache/k4_mainline. Host test: test/run.sh (shipped union object vs the known trains). New train: copy its netd.o, offload.o, test.o, clatd.o and dscpPolicy.o (/apex/com.android.tethering/etc/bpf/mainline/, or /cache/k4_mainline/failed_staged_tethering_<obj>.o after a rolled-back update boot) into known/ as <versionCode>_train_<obj>.o, rerun tethering/regen.py --train-progs with every known train's netd.o (a 180-byte-layout train gets its own netd_a52_<versionCode>.o), run test/run.sh, rebuild.
